FUN_00444178 @0x444178 (skidmark-quad builder): the packed corner locals
(local_3e..local_16, high-half shorts of the 4 assembled skid vertices) are
read back with SIGNED shifts in the original:
  44454e: 8b 45 9e  mov -0x62(%ebp),%eax
  444551: c1 f8 10  sar $0x10,%eax         ; -> 0x74c4e0 (GTE vr input)
  444677: c1 f8 10  sar $0x10,%eax         ; -> 0x74c504
  (same pattern for all vertex components feeding GTERPS/GTERPT)
Ghidra declared the locals undefined4 (unsigned), so the C `local_XX >> 0x10`
zero-extended. Negative corner components (corner table @0x7959a8 holds values
like -75/-160/-291) turned into huge positives; the GTE screen-clamps collapsed
all four corners of every skid quad to ONE point, so our skidmark trapezoids
were drawn degenerate while the reference draws real quads. Visible as the
cf49+ "shadow trapezoid" framebuffer divergence of the L9 attract race (12911
px at cf49; prim 0x795e38 sxy all (634,312) vs ref's 4 distinct corners).
Fix: cast the 11 packed-local high-half reads (int), register-for-register
with the sar semantics.

